lines=['# MVT: closed P0/F128/F256 six-source comparison','', '**Finding:** F256 accelerates CH more strongly than F128, while DH remains slower than its own P0. CH P0/F128/F256 cycles are26,581,175 /25,573,002 /24,342,928; DH34,687,540 /35,332,620 /35,093,446. F256 DH reciprocal-cycle speedup is0.988434 (1.1702% more cycles than P0), while CH speedup is1.091946. Same-F CH/DH is0.693660: DH still takes44.1628% more cycles. I=0.905203 is worse than P0 and F128; do not describe it as a relative DTC improvement.','', 'This is six closed matched sources for one frozen input, including both newly authorized CH runs after natural strict/true164/native-restore acceptance. It does not use current scan observations as performance, select per-program best variants for a GM, alter historical scientific identities, modify original results, or start any model. The previous MVT F128 packet and all members remain byte-identical.','', '## Identity and actual kernel contract','', 'Full input `f437190767aaed4921e11e6b85f80fb3348da90ec0f18fa8fa1bdfcd76ae3079`; actual fixed contract/strict proof/full declared-body qualification: K1 `_Z11mvt_kernel1PfS_S_`,71,380,992active-thread instructions; K2 `_Z11mvt_kernel2PfS_S_`,74,285,056. Both stream0, grid(16,1,1),block(256,1,1),16CTAs; total145,666,048instructions/32CTAs. Bounded4096-byte headers corroborate the actual input\'s own geometry, not an assumption from the other matrix-vector programs.','', 'Core `9eedb3131937748f0492fa83aad37d3691118d70`, Framework `02775fd795cde5aae1480d81cee6eb481d0a08f4`, binary SHA `02a289360b42a573832698c978f21ad2125182a453067a35be60410f1eb8888d`. Original CH-P0/DH-P0/DH-F128/DH-F256 are selected by exact full digest/cell/profile from ORIGINAL_REFERENCE_INDEX.json; reference aliases remain disclosed. New CH points remain STAGEII_AUTHORIZED_CH. No R2/IR/EP/PQPS result is substituted.','', 'Prior MVT F128 manifest `062f7262459e8bac45adeee494038a85b63b73319fe19db7b1dbde3150a440ae` and all its members were rechecked unchanged; its four RESULT identities exactly match this six-source package. Both new CH results were independently requalified with the frozen read-only strict/archive/native-restore adapter.','', '## Performance: relative versus own-design changes','',tab(['Profile','CH cycles','DH cycles','S_CH','S_DH','CH_F/DH_F','I=S_DH/S_CH','DH extra cycles vs CH %'],[[p,by['CH',p]['cycles'],by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_CH']for x in perf if x['profile']==p),1 if p=='P0'else next(x['S_DH']for x in perf if x['profile']==p),by['CH',p]['cycles']/by['DH',p]['cycles'],1 if p=='P0'else next(x['I']for x in perf if x['profile']==p),100*(by['DH',p]['cycles']/by['CH',p]['cycles']-1)]for p in['P0','F128','F256']]),'', 'CH F256 reduces cycles8.4204% relative to CH-P0; DH F256 increases cycles1.1702% relative to DH-P0. Compared with F128, F256 saves1,230,074CH cycles and239,174DH cycles, yet CH improves more, so same-F DTC relative performance deteriorates further. The recovery in DH relative to F128 must not be mislabeled a positive DH result versus P0.','',tab(['Source','K1 cycles','K2 cycles','K1 delta vs own P0','K2 delta vs P0'],[[c+'-'+p,by[c,p]['kernels'][0]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][1]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][0]['cycles']-by[c,'P0']['kernels'][0]['cycles'],by[c,p]['kernels'][1]['cycles']-by[c,'P0']['kernels'][1]['cycles']]for c,p in pairs]),'', 'F256 vs P0: CH total-2,238,247cycles =K1-2,236,059 plusK2-2,188; DH total+405,906 =K1+408,100 plusK2-2,194. F256 vs F128: CH K1-1,227,582/K2-2,492 and DH K1-237,735/K2-1,439. Most change is K1; K2 is small but not exactly unchanged.','', 'The fixed source candidate maps K1 to x1+=A*y1 (matrix row stride across lanes) and K2 to x2+=A^T*y2 (lane-contiguous matrix elements), with separate input/output vectors (`mvt.cu:109-136;launch149-177`). It does not make the second kernel consume the first kernel\'s vector as ATAX does. This conditional source mapping is consistent with an access-direction contrast, but no source-derived recurrence or address overlap is treated as a measured hit/merge or proven bottleneck. Capture-time ELF/numeric binding remains unresolved.','', '## Cumulative traffic and visible retries','', 'L2 GLOBAL accepted read/miss units are32-byte sectors: accepted excludes reservation retries, GLOBAL misses=MISS+SECTOR_MISS. All-L2 misses include other access types. DRAM read/write values are issued32-byte atoms summed across20controllers. Keep these populations separate even when GLOBAL misses and DRAM read atoms coincide in these runs. Cumulative last stream0snapshots span both replay kernels; do not sum snapshots.','']
